<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal down, oil steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal down, oil steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were down further by 100-150 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Friday. Arrivals improved and buying support from soybean processing plants was poor. The undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in restricted trading activity. Demand and supply were both narrowly ranged. The undertone was weak.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was down by $5 rupees per tonne to $295 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) at India's west coast ports in export. There was no demand in the market. Rapeseed extraction was also down to $108-109 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 3,725-3,750 rupees per tonne FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
